From 172913b58230a8205c43b2b2186d05098eefa2f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 17:33:08 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 20/21] panel(sensors): convert popover to native Singularity
 widgets

Replaces the hand-built Gtk.Box+Label+Button tree in SensorsIndicator with
Singularity.Widgets.PreferencesGroup / PreferencesRow / ActionRow, the same
controls the rest of the desktop surface (desktop_page, calendar_view) uses
for grouped lists. The compact panel-bar chip stays as a single Pango
markup Label -- see the inline comment for why native Chip is wrong for that
slot.

Behaviour preserved:
  * every severity threshold, MAX_ROWS_PER_GROUP cap, polling interval,
    schema-key guard, map/unmap gate, hidden_for_unavailable flag, and
    synchronous-refresh-on-popover-open path is byte-for-byte the same.
  * The heat bar stays a raw Gtk.DrawingArea owned by make_heat_bar(). A
    native/themed widget (Gtk.LevelBar) was tried here before -- its
    battery-style level-low/level-high semantics paint every short bar red
    regardless of temperature, and fighting that with theme overrides was
    worse than owning the pixels. Deliberately the exception to the
    "use the native/themed thing" rule this commit otherwise enforces.

Three decisions worth flagging:

  1. Toggle (Grouped/Ungrouped): ActionRow, not SelectionRow or
     SwitchRow. The original Button label doubled as the current state
     ("Grouped" / "Ungrouped") so glancing at it told you which mode you
     were in -- an explicit design goal of the existing toggle, not an
     accident. ActionRow's title IS that same "label doubles as state"
     contract; clicking the row updates the title in place, matching
     SwitchRow's row-activation pattern. SelectionRow was rejected
     because its whole model is "expand to pick": the value lives behind
     a click, which contradicts the "current state visible without
     opening anything" requirement.

  2. Per-row container: PreferencesRow with set_child(custom Box). Each
     row carries a name label (hexpand, ellipsize), an optional heat
     DrawingArea, and a value label with its severity CSS class -- the
     severity styling stays on the value label inside our custom Box, not
     on the PreferencesRow itself, because PreferencesRow applies its own
     colour to the title area via .title and would fight
     warning/error/dim-label. Heat bar still goes through the standard
     suffix slot via a horizontal Box child.

  3. Compact panel-bar chip: stays a single Pango markup Label. Native
     Singularity.Widgets.Chip is a tab pill (close button, drag-and-drop,
     padding) -- chrome-heavy in the wrong direction for a 4-metric
     summary that has to fit next to the clock. The markup Label
     already gives each metric its own colour and lives at the
     bottom of the pixel budget; converting to even one Chip would push
     the clock off the bar on real hardware. Documented inline so the
     next reader does not redo this evaluation.

Verified:
  * Build: singularity-opt.tgz produced via cix-installer/build/build-
    singularity.sh; the staged binary contains singularity_sensors_
    indicator_build_row and the three widget classes (ActionRow,
    PreferencesGroup, PreferencesRow) are linked from libsingularity.
  * Visual confirmation: deferred to a human on O6N. The widget cannot be
    meaningfully unit-tested (it reads live sysfs/hwmon and renders GTK);
    no automated harness exists for it.
